    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "IRDAI headquarters is located in Hyderabad, unlike RBI and SEBI which are based in Mumbai.",
        "SEBI was established as a non-statutory body in 1988 but gained statutory powers via the SEBI Act in 1992.",
        "RBI was established on April 1, 1935 based on the recommendations of the Hilton Young Commission."
      ],
      "id": "s39wl41"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "RBI acts as the central bank regulating monetary policy, currency issuance, and commercial banking under the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "SEBI regulates the securities and capital markets to protect investors and ensure orderly market operations under the SEBI Act, 1992.",
        "IRDAI functions as the autonomous statutory authority regulating and promoting insurance and re-insurance industries under the IRDA Act, 1999.",
        "While RBI and SEBI maintain their primary headquarters in Mumbai, IRDAI is uniquely headquartered in Hyderabad."
      ],
